1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Integra CRM — App ID 865904982715022
Permission requested: business_management (Advanced Access)

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Our platform. Business customers sign in here
to manage their WhatsApp conversations.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Signing in with the test account
provided in this submission.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
No WhatsApp number connected to this account yet.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Starting Embedded Signup to connect the customer's
own WhatsApp Business account.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Facebook Login for Business dialog.
The customer signs in with their own account.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The customer reviews and grants
the permissions our app requests.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Business portfolio selection.
This step requires business_management.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
The WhatsApp Business Account is created under the customer's
own portfolio (WABA Sharing model). We never take ownership of it.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,000
The customer enters and verifies
their WhatsApp Business phone number.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Onboarding complete. The dialog returns the WhatsApp
Business Account ID and the phone number ID.

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Back in our app: we subscribed our app to the account
and listed its phone numbers, using the customer's token.

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The connected number, with its Phone ID and WABA ID.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The customer can now message
their own customers from our platform.

15
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
With Standard Access this flow only works for people who hold a role
in our app. Advanced Access is what lets real business customers connect.
